From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:10:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-store): the browser store in React Native, on
 kv-sqlite linked into the app

`@aztec-labs/kv-store/sqlite-opfs` gains a react-native export condition: the
same API (AztecSQLiteOPFSStore.open, listStores, deleteStore, ...) over
AztecKvSqliteStore, whose Kv service is the library @aztec-foundation/react-native
links into the app, reached through JSI. Each store is a database file in the
app's data directory, in the per-store directory layout the browser uses in
OPFS, and one open store holds a directory at a time (SqlitePoolBusyError), as
in the browser. So the PXE and the embedded wallet open their stores unchanged.

The package imports (#msgpackr, #ordered-binary) get react-native targets that
are files of the package, which is all Metro resolves them to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

diff --git a/yarn-project/kv-store/package.json b/yarn-project/kv-store/package.json
